// runtime/stdlib/discriminant_error.kara
//
// The `Err` payload of the auto-generated `TryFrom[intN]` on a C-like
// `#[repr(intN)]` enum — design.md § Enum Discriminant Runtime Surface, which
// specifies it verbatim as "a prelude error type (`enum DiscriminantError {
// OutOfRange { value: D } }`, parameterized by the repr type)".
// B-2026-08-21-26.
//
// Lives in the prelude so `match UsbClass.try_from(raw)` needs no import,
// parallel to `AllocError` / `IoError`. `D` is the source enum's repr type, so
// the value that failed to map comes back at the width it was read at rather
// than widened to `i64` — a `#[repr(u8)]` enum reports a `u8`.
//
// One variant, not two: the only way an `intN -> enum` conversion fails is a
// value outside the declared set. It derives the same set as `AllocError`,
// whose payload is likewise a single integer, so an out-of-range value is
// printable and comparable in a test without a hand-written `impl`.

#[derive(Debug, Display, Eq, Copy)]
enum DiscriminantError[=D] {
    OutOfRange { value: D },
}
